/*
 * Declares the TupleFieldAccessValue class.
 *
 * TupleFieldAccessValue represents a field access inside a tuple value. Unlike
 * named records, tuples have anonymous fields, so each element is accessed by
 * index rather than by name (e.g. `tuple._0`). The index determines which
 * component of the tuple is extracted.
 *
 * The lvalue-ness of the result follows the tuple operand: if the tuple itself
 * is an lvalue, the accessed element is also an lvalue; otherwise it is not
 * assignable.

 *
 * <hr>
 * 
 * @Package: ymirc        
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::fields::tuple
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/fields/tuple.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created (YYYY-MM-DD): 2026-03-02
 * @Copyright (C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
